# Proactive recall (optimized)

Surface useful stored knowledge **without being asked**. Optimize for speed and
low noise: few lookups, early stop, no repeats.

## Skip entirely (efficiency)

Do **not** run recall when:

- The turn is trivial (typo, yes/no, one-line fix, pure code edit with no domain choice).
- You already surfaced recall for this same task/topic in this chat.
- `project-kickoff` or `cross-project-awareness` already loaded the same cards/facts
  this turn — reuse that; do not re-read.

## Timing

- **Once** at task start, or when the topic **clearly changes**.
- Never every message. Never “I checked and found nothing”.

## Lookup budget (cheap → expensive; stop at 2–3 useful items)

| Priority | Source | Cost rule |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `life/profile/core.md` in the vault (if reachable) | One short file only |
| 2 | One matching `.cursor/catalog/projects/<name>.md` and, if needed, one `links.md` skim | Only projects named or clearly implied by the task |
| 3 | One relevant `system/personal-data/` sheet **or** one `life/` / `work/` note | Open a sheet only if the task touches that area (home, garden, …) |
| 4 | `work/attention/current.md` | Only if the task is planning / priorities / “what next” |
| 5 | Chat archive search | **Last resort**, Mac only, and only if 1–4 are thin. One `chat_archive.py search` with 1–3 keywords. Never open `cloud_safe: false` off the Mac. |

Hard cap: **at most four reads** for recall in one turn. Prefer zero archive calls.

Vault path: checkout under home that contains `system/GLOBAL_INSTRUCTIONS.md`.
If unreachable (Cloud / iPhone): use catalog in the current repo only; skip vault and archive.

## Delivery

- At most **2–3** facts or pointers, a few lines, then continue the real work in the same reply.
- Format: short bullets (“Già in vault: …”, “Catalogo: …”) — no preamble.
- If nothing relevant: **silence**.
- Never delay the main task for deeper search.
- New durable fact found only in chat/archive → write via `fact-capture`, do not paste a transcript.

## Never

- Invent memory.
- Dump transcripts.
- Re-state standing chat rules he already lives by (Italian replies, etc.) unless the task needs them.
- Parallel “full vault scan” or multi-query archive fishing.
